 Measure sticky feedback's actual bottom when exposing the live focused control; also measure a sticky footer's top when it bounds the reading area. Missions keeps heading and feedback in one box and uses `attachFocusClearance` for both boundaries. Replay uses the same helper with its operation rail, measured scroll padding and a small textarea scroll margin; keep the first JSON line clear after Tab/PageUp and text reflow while the textarea retains its own scrolling. Do not follow a remembered opener or react to ordinary scrolling. Keep Close above the feedback reachable, and clamp a tall editor's adjustment so its beginning remains visible. Verify painted focus and hit targets; viewport bounds alone cannot detect one element covering another.
 
+For the still-picture workshop, bind the existing `attachFocusClearance` to the dialog and its actual operations rail, opting into `includeControlLabel` so the field purpose stays visible with its native control. Preserve the default control-only behavior for other dialogs. Keep status, Cancel and Close together through pending, settled and failed work; do not replace their operation owner or remove sticky feedback to expose a field. Test the focused file input after successful preview and reverse traversal using the recorded overlapping rectangles for the entire label/control wrapper, then resize with that same live focus. Ordinary scrolling must remain deliberate, closed panels ignore queued work, and disposal removes the observer/listeners and resets insets. Layout alone must not decode, save or change an assignment. Keep mounted geometry checks separate from native painted focus and physical input; see [the workshop guide](../../../docs/still-media-workshop.md).
+
+Prompt: “After previewing a chosen image, reverse-traverse to the original file picker at 390×844, rotate to short landscape, and verify both its label and control clear the measured status rail without changing focus or media. During a held preview keep Cancel visible and authoritative; close/dispose before a queued layout pass and preserve original bytes. Record actual browser bounds separately from the source regression.”
+
 For Controller Apply, capture focus ownership before disabling the initiating action. Native blur to body does not by itself relinquish ownership; subsequent user input, focus choice, hidden document or window blur does. Restore the existing Edit action only on current successful completion, clean up observers on abort/settlement, and retain transaction and binding identity. Native evidence must identify the active element/action, `:focus` and next Tab destination: unnamed buttons can have an empty ID while correctly focused.
 
 Check the active top-layer owner as well as viewport bounds. Craft feedback uses its original renderer status node inside Missions while selection or direct briefing is open; restore that exact node on actual close/disposal and ignore a queued close from an earlier visit. Keep one presenter and the renderer's existing load-token guards. Cosmetic readiness must not block Deploy or create a second cancellation owner. Verify the sticky slot with real selector changes at portrait/landscape and Large text.
